Project Description

This project analyzes sales performance and customer behavior for Green Cart Ltd., a UK based e commerce company specializing in eco friendly 
household products. The objective is to support the Q2 performance review by delivering clear, data driven insights that inform marketing, pricing, 
and operational decisions.

The project begins with loading, cleaning, and validating three core datasets covering sales transactions, product details, and customer profiles. 
You standardize inconsistent text fields, correct data types, handle missing values, remove duplicates, and validate numeric fields to ensure 
data accuracy and reliability. Cleaned datasets are then merged into a single analytical table that preserves all sales transactions.

Feature engineering plays a central role in this analysis. You create revenue and timing based features, segment products by price bands, 
measure time from product launch to purchase, identify delayed deliveries, and extract customer email domains. These features enable deeper 
analysis of purchasing behavior, product performance, and operational efficiency.

Using the merged dataset, the project produces summary tables that highlight weekly revenue trends by region, product category performance, 
customer behavior by loyalty tier, delivery outcomes across regions and price bands, and payment method preferences. Visual analysis supports 
these summaries through clearly labeled charts that reveal trends, comparisons, and relationships in the data.

The final deliverable answers key business questions, including which product categories and regions generate the most revenue, 
whether discounts drive higher sales volume, which loyalty tiers deliver the greatest value, where delivery delays are most common, 
and how customer signup patterns relate to purchasing activity. Optional stretch analysis extends the work to identify high risk or 
underperforming products and early customer behavior patterns.

Deliverables include a well structured Jupyter Notebook documenting the full analytical workflow and a concise PDF report that translates 
findings into actionable business insights. Together, they demonstrate your ability to manage complex datasets, apply analytical reasoning, 
and communicate results that directly support commercial decision making.
